Proposal (video workstream, 2026-11-19): RunVideo takes the verification clip's captions, card-less chapters and
the R2 keys of its action log and edit list (docs/proposals/video.md V2, V3).

pickfit/schema.py and schema/ are protected in a loop session (scripts/loop_guard.py), so the change is here for the
coordinator to review and apply:

    git apply loop/proposals/video-captions.patch
    uv run python scripts/export_schema.py --check     # schema/software.v1.json is in the patch too

What it adds, all optional, so every record written before validates unchanged:

- VideoChapter.raw / raw_s: the unedited recording a chapter's first segment comes from, and where in it.
- VideoCaption {start_s, end_s, text} and RunVideo.captions: the clip's caption cues (served as WebVTT).
- VideoSource {key, sha256} and RunVideo.actions / RunVideo.edit_list: <slug>/<stem>.actions.json and
  <slug>/<clip stem>.json in the videos bucket.
- The chapter rule accepts a clip with no cards (every chapter a feature, the first at 0) beside the old shape (a
  first and a last card, feature null); captions must rise and end by the clip's end.

Until it is applied, pickfit/verify/video.py writes a card-less clip's video field without chapters or captions
(run_video checks RunVideo.model_fields), and tests/test_video_actions.py skips the test that needs it. Checked with
the draft loaded in memory (no protected file written): tests/test_video_actions.py, test_verify_video*.py,
test_web_video.py, test_index.py, test_i18n.py and test_schema.py pass; test_committed_schema_files_match_models only
once the committed schema/software.v1.json is the one in this patch (it was rendered from the draft).

